Z||000000||RobertVol||10-01-2000||07:31 PM||||OK guys! <P>I know we have many threads on this but never really paid attention  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> sorry.<P>Anyway here goes<P>I found a small manifold leak and now also a cracked mount. I think from leaking from above manifold. Now the question is headers<P>Who makes the best? Chris West, Focoa? <P>should I just replace the entire exaust system while I am at it ? I know of the nightmare stories about this whole setup. All opinions needed. Thanks in advance<P>I am assuming also that this is what is causing my constant miss at consistant throttle but correct me if wrong so I can look elswere<BR>OUT <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-01-2000||08:00 PM||||I have seen the FOCOA headers up close and I have to say that those headers are top notch in quality. I would have to say that the FOCOA headers are the best headers. I f you do get them get them coated.<P>There is a guy on this forum who is having trouble with his Christ west headers. He says they are leaking at the welds. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||10-01-2000||09:20 PM||||I've got the FOCOA headers along with BORLA exhaust on my car.  I can say the headers are excellent quality in construction and fit.  I was even able to fit the stock heat shields around the y-pipe with some minor trimming.  The cooling tube to the alternator needs to be removed and modified (or leave off).<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-01-2000||09:20 PM||||that'd be me... and GT Bastard. I ran the car on the DYNO and lost HP and torque with their install... ok i lost USEABLE hp and tq. i gained HP (4) at 6000rpm but lost through the rest of the entire power band. i'm sure if you have a 3.4 or using them as manifolds for a turbo or s/c install they'd be great. for usable Torque and lots of it.. factory manifolds (ported) stock y pipe, and 2.5" cat, 2.5" muffler (flowmaster 40 series) if you ditch the cat yeah you'll have better sound but you'll lose torque between 4 and 6lbft from 1500- 4500. but they sure look sweet! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||10-01-2000||10:41 PM||||Robert, I don't have any #'s or any thing like that but I bought new stock mainfolds<BR>and had them ported and re-welded. For the money and with all the info I got this seemed to be the best for me at the time with a stock 2.8. That was about 2yrs ago with no problems!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000005||RobertVol||10-02-2000||05:47 PM||||Ok guys ...Thanks for the info..<P>Now one clarification. are you saying you gain with stock manifolds with them ported ? If so I think I might go that way. And if so , were is the best place for price on replacement of the stock manifold. <P>Here is another question..<P>What about the ported manifolds with the Borla exaust? would that be a good way to go? that is if any left. or wait for the next run... ||||reg||1
