Z||000008||Phil||10-03-2000||07:26 PM||||A good welder can really salvage just about condition stock manifold. The one on my 85GT came off in 3 pieces and the other one had about 4 cracks. I just flipped one around bolted the "feet" together and had them welded then I removed the restrictions. Cost $30 and a few hours of grinding.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Terrybogin||10-03-2000||07:42 PM||||If I could get some used manifolds, so I would not have to have so much down time, how much would be a good price to pay? Small cracks and rewelding are not a problem because I would be porting them anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||10-03-2000||08:10 PM||||I think the new ones are about $500.00 for a set. I got mine from a guy that had then seating around in his storage shed for about a year. He bought them to put on his Fiero but sold it before he could put them on, so I got them for a good price with some other parts. The stock one's can't be that bad<BR>if I get another 12 yrs out of a new set that has been ported then I'm happy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Didn't want to take the chance on used ones??<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
